      "mergeID": "66a26d500d02ca872c812e31",
      "mergedPostDetails": "There is no way to perform the gestures that VRChat has bound to the palm-up thumb pinch on either hand because they are overridden by the headset's system gestures.\n\nOn Quest, pinching with the thumb on your right hand with your palm up pauses the current app and opens the system menu, and in some software (Virtual Desktop) doing the same on the left hand opens the SteamVR dash. This makes it impossible to perform either action in VRChat, also making it impossible to even complete the hand tracking tutorial.\n\n*It is totally bizarre to me that no one at VRChat thought to test this update on a Quest headset lol (what other headsets even have hand tracking?).*\n\nI see a few possible solutions to this issue:\n\n1. Allow us to reorder/rebind the hand tracking gestures, *(I'd gladly sacrifice something like mute toggle for being able to open the in-game menu)*\n\n2. Allow the thumb-pinch gestures to work with the palm facing away *(won't trigger system gesture)*",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1481] Quest system gestures override VRChat gestures (can't open menu with hand tracking)",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "66a19faf2a9ceb76af1f84bc",
